      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): read resolved userToken with env fallback in channel type resolution",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`resolveSlackConversationInfo()` uses `account.config.userToken` to resolve the token for Slack API calls. `account.config.userToken` only contains the raw config value — it does **not** include the `SLACK_USER_TOKEN` environment variable fallback.\n\nUsers who set `SLACK_USER_TOKEN` env var without also configuring `channels.slack.accounts.<id>.userToken` in the config file get an empty token, causing channel type resolution to silently fall back to `\"unknown\"` for non-DM channels.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `channel-type.ts:88`: `account.config.userToken` → `account.userToken`\n- `account.userToken` is the resolved value that includes env fallback (`configUser ?? envUser`)\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Unit tests (7/7 passed):**\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  7 passed (7)\n```\n\n**Lint:** `npx oxlint` — no errors\n\n**Type check:** `pnpm tsgo` — no errors\n\n**Real behaviour proof (hostname + timestamp + before/after):**\n```\nHost: LIN-66D8BD4EA2C\nPID: 130921\nTime: 2026-07-10T06:23:22.511Z\n\n=== Bug Reproduction: env-only userToken ===\n\nScenario: User sets SLACK_USER_TOKEN env var, no config userToken\nConfig value (account.config.userToken): undefined\nResolved value (account.userToken): \"xoxp-...cdef\"\n\n--- Before fix (account.config.userToken) ---\n  token = EMPTY ❌\n  → channel type API call SKIPPED, always returns \"unknown\"\n\n--- After fix (account.userToken) ---\n  token = SET ✅\n  → channel type API call PROCEEDS, returns correct type\n```\n\n## Review\n\n- Manually reviewed and verified\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
        "branch": "fix/slack-channel-type-user-token-env",
